.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt JOTAIN-SITE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jotain-site
.Nd Static site for the Jotain Emacs configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm just
.Op Cm build | test | serve | ds-sync
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The site presents the Emacs configuration in
.Pa etc/emacs
as a landing page and a set of generated references.
The landing page looks like an Emacs frame.
It has a tab bar with three buffers, a mode line, and an
.Ql I-search
minibuffer over the sections of the page.
The design uses the Jylhis design system.
.Pp
The committed
.Pa public/
directory holds only the landing page, the shared CSS and JavaScript,
and the vendored design assets.
The Nix build in
.Pa package.nix
adds the generated content.
.Pp
The generated content is:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /docs/
Each
.Pa docs/**/*.mdx
page of
.Pa etc/emacs ,
ordered by
.Pa docs/docs.json .
.It Pa /manual/
The Info manual as HTML, and as
.Pa emacs-config.info .
.It Pa /man/
.Xr emacs-config 7
and the manual pages of the Emacs build.
.It Pa /info/emacs/ , Pa /info/elisp/
The GNU Emacs and Emacs Lisp manuals of the Emacs revision that the
configuration builds.
.It Pa /options/
The Nix module option reference.
.It Pa /help/packages/
The reference for each package, from the
.Ql ;;; @doc
markers in the Lisp files.
.It Pa /help/api/
The docstring reference for each bundled package.
.It Pa /packages/
Search over
.Pa /help/api/ .
.El
.Pp
The preview variant of the build omits
.Pa /help/api/
and
.Pa /packages/ .
The
.Va baseHref
argument of
.Pa site.nix
prefixes every internal absolute URL.
Its default is
.Pa /jotain .
Pass an empty string to serve the site from a root.
.Sh COMMANDS
Run these commands in this directory.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic just build
Build the full site into
.Pa result/public .
.It Ic just test
Build the preview variant and run the
.Ql ds-in-sync
check.
.It Ic just serve
Build the site and serve it at
.Pa http://localhost:8080/jotain/ .
.It Ic just ds-sync
Copy the design assets of the in-tree design system
.Pq Pa lib/design
into
.Pa public/ds .
Workers Builds deploys the committed copy.
Run it when the
.Ql ds-in-sync
check fails.
.El
.Pp
The Nix attributes are
.Ql local.packages.jotain-site ,
.Ql local.checks.jotain-site-build ,
and
.Ql local.checks.jotain-site-ds-in-sync .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa package.nix
Builds the site and the checks.
It takes the Emacs sources from
.Pa ../../etc/emacs
by path.
.It Pa site.nix
Assembles the site from
.Pa public/
and the generated references.
.It Pa public/
The deployed shell.
.It Pa public/ds/
Design system CSS and self-hosted fonts.
Never edit these files.
.It Pa wrangler.jsonc
The assets-only Worker that serves
.Pa public/ .
.El
.Sh CONVENTIONS
.Bl -bullet
.It
No hex literals in
.Pa public/css/site.css .
Colors come from the custom properties in
.Pa public/ds/tokens.css ,
so both modes stay in step.
.It
Some places cannot use a custom property and hold copies of token values:
the
.Ql theme-color
meta elements in
.Pa public/index.html ,
the page template in
.Pa site.nix ,
and
.Pa public/favicon.svg .
Update all of them when the theme changes.
.It
The style sheets for generated markup pin the heading elements to the
mono font.
An unstyled heading would use the large display face of the design system.
.It
Print (light) is the
.Ql :root
mode.
Negative (dark) is
.Ql data-mode="dark"
on the
.Ql html
element.
.It
The fonts are self-hosted.
The site makes no third-party requests.
.El
.Sh DEPLOYMENT
A service-mode static site.
Cloudflare Workers Builds watches green
.Ql main
and deploys
.Pa public/
as the
.Ql jotain-site
Worker.
CI
.Pq Pa .github/workflows/sites.yml
only checks the build.
.Pp
Workers Builds has no Nix.
It cannot build the generated pages, so it deploys only the committed shell.
To publish the full site, build
.Ql local.packages.jotain-site
and deploy the
.Pa public/
directory of the result with
.Xr wrangler 1 .
.Pp
Connect the Worker to Workers Builds once, as
.Xr jylhis-deploying-static-sites 7
describes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr emacs-config 7 ,
.Xr jylhis-deploying-static-sites 7 ,
.Xr jylhis-manual 7
.Sh HISTORY
The site started inside the Emacs configuration repository and was served
by GitHub Pages at page.jylhis.com/jotain.
It moved to this project with the configuration.
